# Named-character tower/GAL unification · 2026-09-30

The user chose the newer GAL artwork as the shared visual authority and requested that the magic-tower map/HUD follow it. This dated decision supersedes older GAL-only / preserve-tower-character scope notices in the per-character canon and older redraw manifests for the named GAL cast only.

## Shared identity, presentation-specific exports

- Written GAL-SIMPLE canon, approved turnarounds, expression boards and accepted B2 standees remain the design authority
- Map tokens for the 15 named cast members that have enemy-manifest entries use transparent 384×576 derivatives of the accepted B2 standing artwork, or the newly approved canonical merchant standing image
- Alpha bounds are trimmed with a recorded threshold, the whole silhouette is kept, aspect ratio is preserved, and padding is added on a transparent canvas. No new face, costume, equipment or anatomy is synthesized
- Both preferred and fallback map paths use the same canonical identity; obsolete ornate character files remain historical assets and cannot silently reappear as decode fallbacks
- Combat panels, codex cells and HUD previews for all 17 named cast members use the already accepted 512×512 canonical face/expression crops. Whole figures are not squeezed into face-avatar slots
- The hero's accepted identity-matched four-direction hero-v6 chibi remains the directional player token. A one-direction fullbody image must not replace the directional sheet
- The guide has no individual enemy-map entry
- Ordinary generic enemies remain distinct from the named cast; their artwork, stats and mechanics are unchanged
- Environment tiles, structures, items, interactive objects and the separate corruption-repair work keep their existing scope

## Provenance and checks

`05_manifests/named-cast-tower-gal-20260930-v1.json` records every source path/hash, output hash, crop, output size, transform settings, HUD face and former enemy entry. `scripts/build-named-cast-map-art.py` builds only derivatives; `--check` validates source identity and output hashes.

The 26 face crops are governed separately by `avatar-derivatives-v1.2.json` and `canonical-avatars-runtime-20260930-v1.json`; their accepted pixels remain unchanged.

This decision is identity unification, not a generic-foe redesign or a claim that low-resolution UI glyphs gained new detail.
